# .leakcheck-terms — example / template (this .example file IS committed; the real
# .leakcheck-terms lives ONLY in $SOULMOUNT_DATA_DIR and is NEVER committed).
#
# `make init-data` copies this to $SOULMOUNT_DATA_DIR/.leakcheck-terms and walks
# you through filling it. `make leakcheck` fails the build (and the pre-commit
# hook) if ANY line here appears anywhere in the repo tree.
#
# Rules:
#   - One term per line. Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
#   - Matching is case-insensitive, substring.
#   - Add every household-identifying string: given names, nicknames, the city,
#     the street, the bot handle, Telegram chat IDs and user IDs, the robot's
#     chosen name, the YouTube channel/handle, any email or phone.
#   - When in doubt, add it. A leak is a stop-everything bug (guardrail 5).
#
# Example entries (delete these — they are illustrations, not real):
# alice
# our-street-name
# our-city
# @our_bot_handle
# 123456789
